course: dictionary
lesson: 11280
title: Write, the many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Write is a small word with several meanings. The clues in each sentence tell you which one to use. «Nobody in the family can read or write, and they do not mind.» Here write means putting letters on paper, because reading and writing go together.
explain: Look at «William Wordsworth wrote «I wandered lonely as a cloud»». A poet makes up his words and puts them into writing, so wrote means made up and put into words. When you meet write, ask: is someone making something up, or sending something to someone?
explain: The little phrases matter too. «Write down» means write so you will remember. «Write to» means send a letter or message to someone, as Paul wrote letters to churches. Each phrase has its own meaning, so check the words that come after write.
fact: Write is a verb, and its forms are write, writes, wrote, written and writing.
fact: «Write» means to put letters, words or numbers on paper or a screen.
fact: «Write down» means write so you will remember.
fact: «Write to» someone means send them a letter or message.
exercise: Mum says, «Please write down the shopping list so we don't forget.» What does write down mean here? | *Write so you will remember | Throw the list in the bin | Sing the list to the shop | Forget it on purpose
exercise: «Ella wrote to her gran from the seaside.» What does wrote to mean? | *Sent a letter or message to her gran | Went to visit her gran | Painted her gran a picture | Sang a song to her gran
exercise: Your teacher says, «Write the number in words.» What should you do? | Say nothing at all | *Spell the number out in letters, like twelve | Draw twelve dots on the board | Clap twelve times
test: Paul wrote letters to churches. What does wrote mean here? | Built the churches with his hands | Lost the churches | Sang songs to the churches | *Put words on paper and sent them
test: Which word is the past tense of write? | writing | write | writes | *wrote
exam: «Headlines are written to grab you.» What does written mean in this sentence? | *Made up and put into words | Eaten | Lost | Torn up
